              "textField": "Although atherosclerosis is often considered a heart problem, it can occur anywhere in the body, and the disorder that results from that process is named according to the location and the extent of the problem. For instance, if there is severe atherosclerosis in the coronary artery, the disorder is called *coronary artery disease* which can cause angina or if severe, a *myocardial infarction*. If the atherosclerosis occurs in the arteries leading to the brain, it is called *carotid artery disease*, which can cause a *stroke* if it occurs acutely, or if it occurs as a gradual occlusion of the artery, it can cause *vascular dementia*. If the problem occurs in the extremities, it is called *peripheral artery disease* which can cause loss of libido, loss of limbs, GIT problems, chronic kidney disease, aneurysms and other problems."
            },
